            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Gainsborough's Technique and Style</strong><br>\nGainsborough's technique, which involved using brushes with long bristles, allowed for a loose painting style with soft edges. His approach influenced future portrait artists and remains distinctive in his portrayals of the English aristocracy.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Final Years in London</strong><br>\nIn his final years, Gainsborough moved back to London and continued to paint portraits of the elite, including the royal family. However, he also devoted time to his beloved landscapes and experimenting with printmaking.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Death and Legacy</strong><br>\nGainsborough died in 1788, but his art has left a lasting impact. He is celebrated as a major English portrait and landscape painter whose innovative techniques contributed significantly to the art world.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
